{"step_index":21,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:52:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T22:22:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T22:22:44+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/find-skill-repo/all%20github%20repos/speech-to-speech/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 629\nTotal Bytes: 26962\nShowing lines 150 to 300\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n150: \r\n151: This installs the package in editable mode and makes the `speech-to-speech` CLI available.\r\n152: \r\n153: ## Supported Components\r\n154: \r\n155: | Component | Backend | Platforms | Install |\r\n156: |---|---|---|---|\r\n157: | VAD | [Silero VAD v5](https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad) | all | built-in |\r\n158: | STT | [Parakeet TDT](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3) (default) | CUDA / CPU through nano-parakeet, Apple Silicon through MLX | built-in |\r\n159: | STT | [Whisper](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/en/model_doc/whisper) through Transformers | CUDA / CPU | built-in |\r\n160: | STT | [Faster Whisper](https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper) | CUDA / CPU | `faster-whisper` |\r\n161: | STT | [Lightning Whisper MLX](https://github.com/mustafaaljadery/lightning-whisper-mlx) | Apple Silicon | `whisper-mlx` |\r\n162: | STT | [MLX Audio Whisper](https://github.com/huggingface/mlx-audio) | Apple Silicon | built-in on macOS |\r\n163: | STT | [Paraformer](https://github.com/modelscope/FunASR) | CUDA / CPU | `paraformer` |\r\n164: | LLM | OpenAI-compatible API (`responses-api`, `chat-completions`) | hosted providers or self-hosted servers | built-in |\r\n165: | LLM | [Transformers](https://huggingface.co/models?pipeline_tag=text-generation&sort=trending) | CUDA / CPU | built-in |\r\n166: | LLM | [mlx-lm](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm) | Apple Silicon | built-in on macOS |\r\n167: | TTS | [Qwen3-TTS](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-CustomVoice) (default) | GGML / CUDA on Linux, mlx-audio on macOS | built-in |\r\n168: | TTS | [Kokoro-82M](https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M) | CUDA / CPU, Apple Silicon | `kokoro` on non-macOS; built-in on macOS |\r\n169: | TTS | [Pocket TTS](https://github.com/kyutai-labs/pocket-tts) | CPU / CUDA | `pocket` |\r\n170: | TTS | [ChatTTS](https://github.com/2noise/ChatTTS) | CUDA / CPU | `chattts` |\r\n171: | TTS | [MMS TTS](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/model_doc/mms) | CUDA / CPU | `facebook-mms` |\r\n172: \r\n173: Select implementations with `--stt`, `--llm_backend`, and `--tts`. Run `speech-to-speech -h` for exact values and backend-specific flags.\r\n174: \r\n175: ## Run Modes\r\n176: \r\n177: | Mode | Transport | Use it when |\r\n178: |---|---|---|\r\n179: | `realtime` (default) | OpenAI Realtime protocol over WebSocket or WebRTC | You are building an app or device against a standard voice API. |\r\n180: | `local` | Your machine's microphone and speakers | You want to talk to the pipeline directly, no client needed. |\r\n181: | `raw-websocket` | Raw PCM over WebSocket | You want a minimal custom client without the Realtime protocol. |\r\n182: | `socket` | Raw PCM over TCP | Models run on a remote server, with a simple microphone/playback client. |\r\n183: \r\n184: ### Realtime Server\r\n185: \r\n186: ```bash\r\n187: export OPENAI_API_KEY=...\r\n188: speech-to-speech\r\n189: ```\r\n190: \r\n191: This is equivalent to:\r\n192: \r\n193: ```bash\r\n194: speech-to-speech \\\r\n195:     --thresh 0.6 \\\r\n196:     --stt parakeet-tdt \\\r\n197:     --llm_backend responses-api \\\r\n198:     --tts qwen3 \\\r\n199:     --qwen3_tts_model_name Qwen/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-CustomVoice \\\r\n200:     --qwen3_tts_speaker Aiden \\\r\n201:     --qwen3_tts_language auto \\\r\n202:     --qwen3_tts_backend ggml \\\r\n203:     --qwen3_tts_non_streaming_mode True \\\r\n204:     --qwen3_tts_mlx_quantization 6bit \\\r\n205:     --model_name gpt-5.4-mini \\\r\n206:     --chat_size 30 \\\r\n207:     --responses_api_stream \\\r\n208:     --enable_live_transcription \\\r\n209:     --mode realtime\r\n210: ```\r\n211: \r\n212: The default model is `gpt-5.4-mini` through the OpenAI Responses API. Override it with `--model_name`, and set `--responses_api_base_url` for another OpenAI-compatible provider or server.\r\n213: \r\n214: ### Local Mac\r\n215: \r\n216: ```bash\r\n217: speech-to-speech --local_mac_optimal_settings\r\n218: ```\r\n219: \r\n220: Optionally with a specific LLM:\r\n221: \r\n222: ```bash\r\n223: speech-to-speech \\\r\n224:     --local_mac_optimal_settings \\\r\n225:     --model_name mlx-community/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-bf16\r\n226: ```\r\n227: \r\n228: This setting:\r\n229: \r\n230: - Adds `--device mps` to use MPS for all models.\r\n231: - Sets Parakeet TDT for STT.\r\n232: - Sets MLX LM as the LLM backend.\r\n233: - Sets Qwen3-TTS for TTS, using `mlx-audio` with the `6bit` MLX variant by default.\r\n234: - Sets `--mode local`.\r\n235: \r\n236: `--tts pocket` and `--tts kokoro` are also valid on macOS.\r\n237: \r\n238: To compare the MLX quantization variants locally:\r\n239: \r\n240: ```bash\r\n241: python scripts/benchmark_tts.py \\\r\n242:     --handlers qwen3 \\\r\n243:     --iterations 3 \\\r\n244:     --qwen3_mlx_quantizations bf16 4bit 6bit 8bit\r\n245: ```\r\n246: \r\n247: ### Raw WebSocket\r\n248: \r\n249: 1. Run the pipeline in raw WebSocket mode:\r\n250: \r\n251:    ```bash\r\n252:    speech-to-speech --mode raw-websocket --ws_host 0.0.0.0 --ws_port 8765\r\n253:    ```\r\n254: \r\n255: 2. Connect from your client at `ws://<server-ip>:8765`. Send raw audio bytes as 16 kHz, int16, mono PCM and receive generated audio bytes back.\r\n256: \r\n257: ### TCP Socket\r\n258: \r\n259: TCP socket mode is intentionally minimal. It streams raw PCM audio, but does not provide the full Realtime API feature set, including interruption handling, live transcript events, or tool-call events.\r\n260: \r\n261: 1. Run the pipeline on the server:\r\n262: \r\n263:    ```bash\r\n264:    speech-to-speech --mode socket --recv_host 0.0.0.0 --send_host 0.0.0.0\r\n265:    ```\r\n266: \r\n267: 2. Run the client locally to handle microphone input and playback:\r\n268: \r\n269:    ```bash\r\n270:    python scripts/listen_and_play.py --host <IP address of your server>\r\n271:    ```\r\n272: \r\n273: ### Docker\r\n274: \r\n275: Install the [NVIDIA Container Toolkit](https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/install-guide.html), then:\r\n276: \r\n277: ```bash\r\n278: docker compose up\r\n279: ```\r\n280: \r\n281: The compose file starts a llama.cpp server with Gemma 4, starts the TCP socket server, and exposes ports `8080`, `12345`, and `12346`.\r\n282: \r\n283: ## Realtime API\r\n284: \r\n285: Realtime mode supports the OpenAI Realtime protocol over WebSocket and WebRTC, with live transcription and low-latency turn-taking. WebSocket clients connect at `/v1/realtime`:\r\n286: \r\n287: ```python\r\n288: from openai import OpenAI\r\n289: \r\n290: client = OpenAI(\r\n291:     base_url=\"http://localhost:8765/v1\",\r\n292:     websocket_base_url=\"ws://localhost:8765/v1\",\r\n293:     api_key=\"not-needed\",\r\n294: )\r\n295: \r\n296: with client.realtime.connect(model=\"local\") as conn:\r\n297:     conn.send(\r\n298:         {\r\n299:             \"type\": \"session.update\",\r\n300:             \"session\": {\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
