{"step_index":33,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:53:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T22:23:12+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T22:23:12+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/find-skill-repo/all%20github%20repos/ViMax/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 518\nTotal Bytes: 22307\nShowing lines 320 to 518\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n320: Generate multiple images in parallel and select the best consistent image as the first frame through MLLM/VLM to imitate the workflow of human creators.\r\n321: \r\n322: ⚡ **High-efficiency Parallel Shot Generation**\r\n323: \r\n324: Parallel processing for sequential shots captured from the same camera enables highly efficient video production.\r\n325: \r\n326: \r\n327: \r\n328: \r\n329: \r\n330: ### 🤖 <strong>Multi-Agent Video Generation Pipeline</strong>\r\n331: \r\n332: <div align=\"center\">\r\n333:   <table align=\"center\" width=\"100%\" style=\"border: none; border-collapse: collapse;\">\r\n334:     <tr>\r\n335:       <td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 20px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%); border-radius: 15px; color: white; font-weight: bold;\">\r\n336:         🧠 <strong>INPUT LAYER</strong><br/>\r\n337:         📝 Idea & Scripts & Novels • 💭 Natural Language Prompts • 🖼️ Reference Images • 🎨 Style Directives • 🧩 Configs\r\n338:       </td>\r\n339:     </tr>\r\n340:     <tr><td colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\"></td></tr>\r\n341:     <tr>\r\n342:       <td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 15px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b6b 0%, #ee5a24 100%); border-radius: 12px; color: white; font-weight: bold;\">\r\n343:         🧭 <strong>CENTRAL ORCHESTRATION</strong><br/>\r\n344:         Agent Scheduling • Stage Transitions • Resource Management • Retry/Fallback Logic\r\n345:       </td>\r\n346:     </tr>\r\n347:     <tr><td colspan=\"3\" height=\"15\"></td></tr>\r\n348:     <tr>\r\n349:       <td align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 12px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3742fa 0%, #2f3542 100%); border-radius: 10px; color: white; width: 50%;\">\r\n350:         🧾 <strong>SCRIPT UNDERSTANDING</strong><br/>\r\n351:         <small>Character/Environment Extraction • Scene Boundaries • Style Intent</small>\r\n352:       </td>\r\n353:       <td width=\"10\"></td>\r\n354:       <td align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 12px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8c7ae6 0%, #9c88ff 100%); border-radius: 10px; color: white; width: 50%;\">\r\n355:         🎥 <strong>SCENE & SHOT PLANNING</strong><br/>\r\n356:         <small>Storyboard Steps • Shot List • Key Frames & Beats</small>\r\n357:       </td>\r\n358:     </tr>\r\n359:     <tr><td colspan=\"3\" height=\"15\"></td></tr>\r\n360:     <tr>\r\n361:       <td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 15px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00d2d3 0%, #54a0ff 100%); border-radius: 12px; color: white; font-weight: bold;\">\r\n362:         🧪 <strong>VISUAL ASSET PLANNING</strong><br/>\r\n363:         Reference Image Selection • Look/Style Guidance • Prompt Conditioning\r\n364:       </td>\r\n365:     </tr>\r\n366:     <tr><td colspan=\"3\" height=\"15\"></td></tr>\r\n367:     <tr>\r\n368:       <!-- Swapped: ASSET INDEXING is now on the left -->\r\n369:       <td align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 12px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e056fd 0%, #f368e0 100%); border-radius: 10px; color: white; width: 50%;\">\r\n370:         🗂️ <strong>ASSET INDEXING</strong><br/>\r\n371:         <small>Frames/Refs Catalog • Embeddings • Retrieval for Reuse</small>\r\n372:       </td>\r\n373:       <td width=\"10\"></td>\r\n374:       <!-- Swapped: CONSISTENCY & CONTINUITY is now on the right -->\r\n375:       <td align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 12px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffa726 0%, #ff7043 100%); border-radius: 10px; color: white; width: 50%;\">\r\n376:         ♻️ <strong>CONSISTENCY & CONTINUITY</strong><br/>\r\n377:         <small>Character/Environment Tracking • Ref Matching • Temporal Coherence</small>\r\n378:       </td>\r\n379:     </tr>\r\n380:     <tr><td colspan=\"3\" height=\"15\"></td></tr>\r\n381:     <tr>\r\n382:       <td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 15px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #26de81 0%, #20bf6b 100%); border-radius: 12px; color: white; font-weight: bold;\">\r\n383:         ✂️ <strong>VISUAL SYNTHESIS & ASSEMBLY</strong><br/>\r\n384:         Image Generation • Best-Frame Selection • First/Last-Frame→Video • Cut & Timeline Assembly\r\n385:       </td>\r\n386:     </tr>\r\n387:     <tr><td colspan=\"3\" height=\"15\"></td></tr>\r\n388:     <tr>\r\n389:       <td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\" style=\"padding: 20px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #045de9 0%, #09c6f9 100%); border-radius: 15px; color: white; font-weight: bold;\">\r\n390:         🚀 <strong>OUTPUT LAYER</strong><br/>\r\n391:         🖼️ Frames • 🎞️ Clips & Final Videos • 📜 Logs • 📦 Working Directory Artifacts\r\n392:       </td>\r\n393:     </tr>\r\n394:   </table>\r\n395: </div>\r\n396: \r\n397: \r\n398: \r\n399: \r\n400: \r\n401: \r\n402: ## 🚀Quick Start\r\n403: \r\n404: ### 🖥️ **Environment**\r\n405: \r\n406: ```\r\n407: OS: Linux, Windows\r\n408: ```\r\n409: \r\n410: ### 📥 **Clone and Install**\r\n411: We use uv to manage the environment. For uv installation, please refer to the https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/.\r\n412: ```bash\r\n413: git clone https://github.com/HKUDS/ViMax.git\r\n414: cd ViMax\r\n415: uv sync\r\n416: ```\r\n417: \r\n418: \r\n419: ### 🧠 **Agent TUI**\r\n420: ViMax also provides a minimal TUI for interactive agent-based video creation. Configure the model and API key information in `configs/agent.local.yaml`, including the LLM, image generator, and video generator, as shown below.\r\n421: ```yaml\r\n422: llm:\r\n423:   model_provider: openai\r\n424:   model: <YOUR_LLM_MODEL>\r\n425:   base_url: <YOUR_LLM_BASE_URL>\r\n426:   api_key: <YOUR_API_KEY>\r\n427: \r\n428: image:\r\n429:   model: <YOUR_IMAGE_MODEL>\r\n430:   base_url: <YOUR_IMAGE_BASE_URL>\r\n431:   api_key: <YOUR_API_KEY>\r\n432: \r\n433: video:\r\n434:   model: <YOUR_VIDEO_MODEL>\r\n435:   base_url: <YOUR_VIDEO_BASE_URL>\r\n436:   api_key: <YOUR_API_KEY>\r\n437: ```\r\n438: \r\n439: Then, start the TUI from the ViMax root directory:\r\n440: ```bash\r\n441: vimax tui\r\n442: ```\r\n443: \r\n444: Start a new session or resume an existing one:\r\n445: ```bash\r\n446: vimax tui new\r\n447: vimax tui resume\r\n448: vimax tui resume <session_id>\r\n449: ```\r\n450: \r\n451: You can also keep `configs/agent.local.yaml` empty and provide the same values through environment variables, such as `VIMAX_LLM_API_KEY`, `VIMAX_IMAGE_API_KEY`, and `VIMAX_VIDEO_API_KEY`.\r\n452: \r\n453: ### 🎯 **Usage**\r\n454: main_idea2video.py is used to convert your ideas into videos.\r\n455: You need to configure the model and API key information in the configs/idea2video.yaml file, including three parts—the chat model, the image generator, and the video generator, as shown below\r\n456: ```yaml\r\n457: chat_model:\r\n458:   init_args:\r\n459:     model: google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025\r\n460:     model_provider: openai\r\n461:     api_key: <YOUR_API_KEY>\r\n462:     base_url: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\r\n463: \r\n464: image_generator:\r\n465:   class_path: tools.ImageGeneratorNanobananaGoogleAPI\r\n466:   init_args:\r\n467:     api_key: <YOUR_API_KEY>\r\n468: \r\n469: video_generator:\r\n470:   class_path: tools.VideoGeneratorVeoGoogleAPI\r\n471:   init_args:\r\n472:     api_key: <YOUR_API_KEY>\r\n473: \r\n474: working_dir: .working_dir/idea2video\r\n475: ```\r\n476: \r\n477: Then, provide a simple yet thoughtful idea and the corresponding creative requirements in main_idea2video.py.\r\n478: ```bash\r\n479: idea = \\\r\n480: \"\"\"\r\n481: If a cat and a dog are best friends, what would happen when they meet a new cat?\r\n482: \"\"\"\r\n483: user_requirement = \\\r\n484: \"\"\"\r\n485: For children, do not exceed 3 scenes.\r\n486: \"\"\"\r\n487: style = \"Cartoon\"\r\n488: ```\r\n489: \r\n490: main_script2video.py generates a video based on a specific script.\r\n491: You similarly need to set up the API configuration in configs/script2video.yaml file. Then, provide a scene script and the corresponding creative requirements in main_script2video.py, as shown below.\r\n492: ```python\r\n493: script = \\\r\n494: \"\"\"\r\n495: EXT. SCHOOL GYM - DAY\r\n496: A group of students are practicing basketball in the gym. The gym is large and open, with a basketball hoop at one end and a large crowd of spectators at the other end. John (18, male, tall, athletic) is the star player, and he is practicing his dribble and shot. Jane (17, female, short, athletic) is the assistant coach, and she is helping John with his practice. The other students are watching the practice and cheering for John.\r\n497: John: (dribbling the ball) I'm going to score a basket!\r\n498: Jane: (smiling) Good job, John!\r\n499: John: (shooting the ball) Yes!\r\n500: ...\r\n501: \"\"\"\r\n502: user_requirement = \\\r\n503: \"\"\"\r\n504: Fast-paced with no more than 20 shots.\r\n505: \"\"\"\r\n506: style = \"Animate Style\"\r\n507: ```\r\n508: \r\n509: \r\n510: ---\r\n511: \r\n512: **🌟 If this project helps you, please give us a Star!**\r\n513: \r\n514: <p align=\"center\">\r\n515:   <em> ❤️ Thanks for visiting ✨ ViMax!</em><br><br>\r\n516: </p>\r\n517: \r\n518: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
